<Defs>

  <!--
    The Last Republic (docs/design/peoples-third.md, the third of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release F";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesF2.cs): what is left of the old planetary government, which collapsed everywhere but
    in a handful of towns that kept the archives, the ration cards and the radio. They hold elections, keep a census and
    broadcast the news as they wish it were. Industrial, on the game's outlander parent; they arise in every age (ariseAges
    0~3), and rise toward the spacer age at a steady pace, their archives holding more than they can build yet (agePace
    9). The Civic Guard wears one uniform, the clearest after the Ashen Banner's: a collar shirt, trousers, a flak vest and
    a helmet, all in civic navy, with issued rifles (the game's) and, with Vanilla Weapons Expanded - Non-Lethal, batons and
    tasers; in another age the age's issue (ageArms: war shirts and spears among the tribes, plate and halberds in the
    medieval age, recon armour and charge rifles in the spacer age). Clerks and citizens wear drab, varied civilian clothes
    with a cap or hat in the Republic's navy. A share are bureaucrats and speakers (the clerks' skills, A RimWorld of Magic's
    bards); with Royalty a propaganda officer or two among the clerks has a psylink (Vanilla Psycasts Expanded's Empath and
    Puppeteer). Their towns: a town hall with its flag, an archive, a ration office and a guardhouse
    (Rimfolk_Plan_RepublicHall). At the gate: a census-taker walks the colony and counts its people
    (Rimfolk_Evt_RepublicCensus); the Republic offers citizenship papers, better terms with its traders and a duty owed
    (Rimfolk_Evt_RepublicPapers); it asks a conscript for a season, who goes to its town and comes back by the world's own
    roads (Rimfolk_Evt_RepublicConscript); and its radio praises or denounces the colony once a season (Peoples/PeoplesF2.cs,
    RepublicRadio). Their ask: a witness for the count of their election (Rimfolk_Mission_RepublicCount). Their founding:
    Clement Ashdown, the postmaster who kept the radio on. Faith (Ideology): loyalty to the Republic, Vanilla Ideology
    Expanded's republic and city builders. Kinds of people: hussars, genies, highmates, Neanderthals, pigskins, the
    Uredde, Åskbarns and Venators, four in five baseliners.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Republic</defName>
    <label>Last Republic</label>
    <description>What is left of the planet's old government: a handful of towns that kept the archives, the ration cards and the radio when everything else fell. The Republic still holds elections, keeps a census of everyone it can count and broadcasts the news every evening, as it wishes it were. Its Civic Guard keeps order in its streets in the same uniform it wore when the Republic had cities.\n\nTheir ways began the winter the capital went dark. The postmaster of a small town, Clement Ashdown, found himself the most senior official still answering the radio, and he would not let it go silent. He read out the old laws each evening, issued ration cards from the post office and called an election in the spring, and towns that heard him began to answer. The Republic still dates its laws from that broadcast. A citizen still wears the Republic's navy somewhere about them, and the Guard wears it all over.\n\nThey are formal, patient and very fond of paperwork, and they speak of the Republic as if it had never fallen. They fear disorder, an uncounted people and a silent radio. Each town is run by its minister, and the Republic by its president.</description>
    <pawnSingular>citizen</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>citizens</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>president</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Republic_Citizen</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Republic</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_RepublicTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Republic</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/RepublicTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.12, 0.18, 0.38)</li>
      <li>(0.22, 0.30, 0.55)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>48</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.5</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.3)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Hussar MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Hussar>
        <Genie MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Genie>
        <Highmate MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Highmate>
        <Neanderthal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Neanderthal>
        <Pigskin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Pigskin>
        <Uredd MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,rimsenal.askbarn">0.02</Uredd>
        <Askbarn MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,rimsenal.askbarn">0.02</Askbarn>
        <DV_Venator MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.venators">0.02</DV_Venator>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Republic Never Fell</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>The Republic never fell: it simply has fewer citizens than it used to. Its laws stand, its census goes on, its elections are held on the day, and every citizen owes it a duty and is owed its protection in turn. Order is kept, the count is kept and the radio is kept on, because a government that stops speaking stops being one. Clement Ashdown, the postmaster who answered the radio the winter the capital went dark, read the old laws aloud every evening until other towns answered, and every law since is dated from that first broadcast.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Loyalist</li>
      <!-- Elections held on the day: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's republic. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Republic</li>
      <!-- Towns kept as the old cities were: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's city builders. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_CityBuilders</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
      <Structure_Ideological MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">3</Structure_Ideological>
      <Structure_Archist MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">1</Structure_Archist>
    </structureMemeWeights>
    <styles>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Christian</li>
    </styles>
    <caravanTraderKinds Inherit="False">
