        <agePace>9</agePace>
        <ageLimit>3</ageLimit>
        <townWord>town</townWord>
        <townWords>towns</townWords>
        <head>minister</head>
        <heir>deputy minister</heir>
        <envoy>census-taker</envoy>
        <trader>quartermaster</trader>
        <courier>dispatch rider</courier>
        <couriers>dispatch riders</couriers>
        <caravanWeight>0.9</caravanWeight>
        <camps>
          <li>Council_Camp_Refugees</li>
          <li>Council_Camp_Market</li>
          <li>Council_Camp_Wardens</li>
        </camps>
        <plan>Rimfolk_Plan_RepublicHall</plan>
        <honours>the census kept, an election held on the day and a radio that never goes silent</honours>
        <fears>disorder in the streets, an uncounted people and the radio gone quiet</fears>
        <sayings>
          <li>The Republic never fell.</li>
          <li>It simply has fewer citizens than it used to.</li>
          <li>Everyone counted, everyone owed.</li>
          <li>Keep the radio on.</li>
          <li>There is a form for that.</li>
        </sayings>
        <townGoods>
          <MealSurvivalPack>10~24</MealSurvivalPack>
          <MedicineIndustrial>6~12</MedicineIndustrial>
          <Steel>60~140</Steel>
          <Cloth>40~90</Cloth>
          <Novel>2~5</Novel>
        </townGoods>
        <herd>
          <li>Horse</li>
        </herd>
        <herdCount>2~4</herdCount>
        <ariseAges>0~3</ariseAges>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release F"): the Civic Guard in one uniform, everyone else in their own
    clothes. A guard wears the issue: a collar shirt, trousers, a flak vest and a simple helmet, all civic navy, the same
    on every guard but for wear and quality, with the Guard's rifles (the game's) and, with Non-Lethal, its batons, tasers
    and tear gas; in another age the age's issue in the same navy (ageArms: Vanilla Factions Expanded - Tribals' war
    shirts and spears, the game's plate and halberds, recon armour and charge rifles). Clerks and the president wear the
    Republic's formal wear: a collar shirt and trousers under the game's and Vanilla Apparel Expanded's jackets, a navy
    bowler for the clerks, a navy greatcoat (the game's duster) for the president. Citizens and the quartermaster dress
    drably and freely, the game's and the mods' everyday clothes, with a cap or hat in civic navy. A share of the clerks
    are speakers (A RimWorld of Magic's bards) and, with Royalty, propaganda officers with a psylink. They carry rations
    and medicine. Without any mod: the game's shirts, trousers, flak vests, helmets, bowlers, dusters, rifles and pistols.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_RepublicKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_Republic</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.04</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>0.02</backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
    <specificApparelRequirements>
